          "start": 307
        },
        "quote": "(b) No person shall occupy any mobile home on the premises of any occupied dwelling or on any lot which is not a part of the premises of any occupied dwelling, either of which is situated outside of an approved mobile home park, except that one visiting mobile home may be parked in an accessory private garage building or in a rear yard in any district for a period of not more than 30 days. (Code 1981 § 25-2. Code 1995 § 98-3.)",
